  "prediction_basis_card_ids": ["C06","C01","C04","C16","C74","C104","C61","C71","C84","C108"],
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "Direct low-F evidence for quaternary ammonium and strongly cationic small molecules: diphemanil methylsulphate showed very low oral bioavailability after a 250 mg oral dose (C06), and DX-9065a showed human oral bioavailability of 2–3% and 2.8 ± 1.5% as a conventional capsule (C01, C04), with 3% in fasted humans (C16).",
      "card_ids": ["C06","C01","C04","C16"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Oral exposure for quaternary ammonium antimuscarinics is low: trospium Cmax values were 1517–2717 pg/mL with AUC24 ~14,900–28,590 pg·h/mL (C74, C104, C61, C71), and glycopyrronium Cmax was 318 pg/mL after a 2 mg oral dose (C84), consistent with low oral systemic exposure.",
      "card_ids": ["C74","C104","C61","C71","C84"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Trospium has high aqueous solubility (>100 mg/mL, C108), so low oral exposure in this class is not solubility-limited; gut-wall evidence shows high efflux ratios for tropane analogs (C195) and ion-pair enhancement needed for propantheline absorption (C193), supporting an absorption/permeability barrier rather than a high-F mechanism.",
      "card_ids": ["C108","C195","C193"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L6 hepatic-clearance records for close analogs ipratropium and tiotropium show low human liver microsomal intrinsic clearance (<7 µL/min/mg; C219, C217, C239) and predicted hepatic clearance of 9.6–12.4 ml/min/kg (C212, C253), indicating hepatic first-pass is not the dominant cause of low F in this class; this does not provide affirmative evidence for F ≥ 20% and does not overturn the absorption-based low prediction.",
      "card_ids": ["C219","C217","C239","C212","C253"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "hepatic_clearance_metabolic_stability",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C212","C253","C219","C217","C239","C243","C205","C248","C251"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement for the exact query molecule.",
    "No query-specific hepatic clearance or metabolic-stability data; L6 records are for close analogs (ipratropium, tiotropium, atropine) in various species and assay systems.",
    "Query formulation, dose, prandial state, and salt form are unspecified.",
    "L3 oral-exposure records for trospium/glycopyrronium/scopolamine lack IV comparators in these cards, so low Cmax/AUC alone does not fully separate absorption from clearance/distribution.",
    "The molecule_property_tool_summary reports neutral fraction 1 despite a quaternary ammonium nitrogen; this inconsistency limits reliance on the physicochemical prior."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted low. Direct low-F evidence for quaternary ammonium/strong-cation small molecules and low oral exposure for quaternary ammonium antimuscarinics support F < 20%. L6 shows low hepatic intrinsic clearance for close analogs, indicating hepatic first-pass is not the main barrier; this is neutral for the endpoint and does not provide affirmative evidence for F ≥ 20%. Keep low with moderate confidence."
}

